{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both tests pass. \n\nThe bug was in `repo/config.py`: `merge_config` used `if override[k]:` to decide whether to apply each override value. That truthiness check skips falsy values (`0`, `\"\"`, `False`, `None`), so setting a config option to `0` or an empty string was silently ignored instead of overriding the base.\n\nFix: assign unconditionally for each key present in `override` — `for k in override` already iterates only keys that exist, so the check was both wrong and redundant.\n\n```python\ndef merge_config(base, override):\n    out = dict(base)\n    for k in override:\n        out[k] = override[k]\n    return out\n```"}]},"session_id":"4059d4f0-b8a7-476f-8587-e2dc3fc6c50a"}
